sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch13-03--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch13-03--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch13-03: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.65" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.65"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.68"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Whether most horns are logarithmic spirals is decidable by curve-fitting on existing scans and photographs, and the methods are standard. The causal clause, a constant ratio of growth on opposite sides, is the geometric meaning Thompson gives the spiral rather than a separate measured growth field. Taxonomic coverage is broad enough for a majority claim about well-collected bovids and incomplete for the family as a whole, and it does not separate growth from later mechanical retardation." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Fit logarithmic, circular, and piecewise spirals to horn centerlines from bovid scans and test whether one angle is constant along the horn. A majority of horns with a stable logarithmic angle would support the geometric claim; a better fit by curves whose curvature changes with length would refute it. Unequal axial growth remains identified with that angle unless increment thicknesses are measured around the base." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Open meshes are biased toward species with skeletal specimens and often lack the keratin sheath.", "Constant unequal growth and some adhesion patterns produce the same logarithmic centerline." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch13-03--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch13-03--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch13-03--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch13-03 by Grok 4.7: 0.72" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch13-03--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch13-03--grok--operationalizability> .
